What is NOT included
---------------------

- Understand-Anything's LLM/agent phase (SKILL.md, agents/,
  compute-batches, merge-batch-graphs, fingerprints, locales, etc.).
- The dashboard and the viewer.
- Any runtime network call: extraction runs 100% locally (node +
  tree-sitter/WASM); npm is only used once, to install the
  vendored/public dependencies (npm install --ignore-scripts).

Re-vendoring procedure (updating to a new upstream commit)
------------------------------------------------------------

1. Clone https://github.com/Egonex-AI/Understand-Anything at the
   desired commit.
2. Diff the 4 .mjs files under skills/understand/ against the ones
   here; if they changed, copy them byte-identical (never edit them
   locally — any adaptation belongs in the extract.mjs wrapper).
3. Rebuild core: in understand-anything-plugin/packages/core, install
   deps and run `tsc` (the "build" script); copy the resulting dist/
   into vendor/core/dist, and package.json with the same single patch
   described above.
4. Re-copy packages/tree-sitter-{dart,swift}-wasm if they changed.
5. Run `npm install --ignore-scripts`, then the golden test:
   `node extract.mjs <repo> --out golden-run ...` + `python
   golden_check.py` against known reference outputs.
6. Update the commit hash/date in this NOTICE, and LICENSE-UA if the
   upstream text changed.
